                <pb facs="0242" n="130" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg130"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/5823: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-06T15:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 6,
                                1919, 3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 6, 12:40
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3500. My 3481, December 2, 4 p.m. I am informally advised by Foreign Office that
                        O’Grady has received not only reiterated instructions
                        <pb facs="0243" n="131" xml:id="pg131"/> to confine his discussions to
                    matters concerning exchange of prisoners but also to refuse even to listen to
                    any representations on any other whatsoever.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
